action_text:
Sitting as the Countywide Planning Authority, hold the first of two public hearings to consider proposed amendments to the Countywide Plan, to include amendments to the Countywide Rules and Countywide Strategies.
The proposed amendments will not impose more restrictive or burdensome land use requirements. Rather, they are intended to expand options available to local governments and streamline the implementation of existing processes.
Bothe the Planners Advisory Committee and the Forward Pinellas Board, in its role as the Pinellas Planning Council, voted unanimously to recommend approval of the amendments as outlined below.
Countywide Plan Strategies
· Updating the introduction
Countywide Rules
· Providing for streamlined Countywide Plan Map amendment submittal and review procedures;
· Implementing recommendations of the Housing Regulatory Toolkit;
· Revising standards for density and intensity bonuses;
· Updating and clarifying provisions for the Target Employment Center category;
· Expanding options for addressing the Multimodal Accessibility Index;
· Revising provisions regarding the Coastal High Hazard Area;
· Clarifying consistency requirements for local plans and codes;
· Revising application provisions;
· Updating eligibility for boundary adjustments;
· Clarifying mailing and notice requirements for Countywide Plan amendments;
· Revising definitions and updating obsolete provisions and references.
